{"title":"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the least positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that the set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive integers beginning with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4f7905a50092d7ff818e56cf44ded4c6309ea1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000\\cdot N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> contains no square of an integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The difference between consecutive integral squares must be greater than 1000. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d91ae277369d56cbd663c3f5f3d72dd2d06e1fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)^2-x^2\\geq1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d763fd11f631eb353bb5eba26ef9b672cb8c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\geq\\frac{999}{2}\\implies x\\geq500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"176\" height=\"37\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0892bb3e1ffbe71b225ba4331f79470d5a4bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=500$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> does not work, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a1553f58de524a9d4121efd999f5b82c529ed3d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7ee6587882fb9da547a60d65d6d05ee0e310d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=x-500$\" width=\"94\" height=\"12\" />. By inspection,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> should end in a number close to but less than 1000 such that there exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9bd1a4e4f78cc34acc8c4ce9075017dd5900a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> within the difference of the two squares. Examine when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c013f6266bed0a478f83b6e0b3a8b707dc94721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f6626e7932addf9e0de8ee1697d4093adae6b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=10\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />. One example way to estimate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4f56670a613c679c0291375283e37df33f3a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> follows. \n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee19f2230cc721282aa8253c8d9b7e5ff8ffbe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2=9$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7bf7eb320f4e69c6caf1ec1c0f37424e1152217.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10=(x+3)^2=x^2+6x+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"19\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is small, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396a361622a7c872a42f98346029e6766f5b54b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10=6x+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/32890efad0d151145f85e499b475078e932165a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1/6\\implies \\sqrt{10}\\approx 19/6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" />. This is 3.16.\n</pre>\n<p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea661c3e2dc0ac0918b98de6689967dadb9326a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\approx 31.6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870127d9d70f5a862982fd8bda82a7a3897d7f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> could be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Add 500 to get the first square and 501 to get the second. Then, the two integral squares are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca36ac8438ae6d88ad487dfa0a27dc808fc85b52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$531^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3b0f8864eb75b84bee75119879bb2a22b0b3f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$532^2$\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />. Checking, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04525d80591cd8f04aa2fd30d40d4e5081ca395b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$531^2=281961$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e5f9297dbfdb360de90aa061921ccccaf7193c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$532^2=283024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283186b64e7ea92fa42081ef65abc9bd6d080664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$282,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> straddles the two squares, which have a difference of 1063. The difference has been minimized, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is minimized <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408718265b939c4659b0cffb3f8f41ac9e321de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=282000\\implies\\boxed{282}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~BJHHar\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let us first observe the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82cf76c497ec62c04f433242f343a4645d2b0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" />, for any arbitrary <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b5205f058a0f55b22ecf025f21108e6b2ed1100c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfaa5db877a3d2850d3102d3309c288ab9c0bcfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)^2-x^2=2x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />. So that means for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b5205f058a0f55b22ecf025f21108e6b2ed1100c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, the difference between that square and the next square have a difference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8fc82e121c01034fef87ac28f73e7d4c0b465c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />. Now, we need to find an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fd948f6ac144938139920aca573f2b6502134b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+1\\ge 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />. Solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c57295191e8cbd6b1f221917e682491072afb5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge \\frac{999}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/650bbfd3736f11e314065e9942159e9e65064623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />. Now we need to find what range of numbers has to be square-free: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c39e05ef603ddb6ac6101e71cb8186d74795b3ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{N000}\\rightarrow \\overline{N999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> have to all be square-free.\nLet us first plug in a few values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to see if we can figure anything out. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0892bb3e1ffbe71b225ba4331f79470d5a4bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=500$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b60d66e17fec05d78ebaa664e5c0e7424099a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=250000$\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636aa953161c6ab67fbb246853b19f6af42f6e46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)^2=251001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" />. Notice that this does not fit the criteria, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/5/085582a9ce8c4388675b5ecd883cc1f9f06789d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250000$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> is a square, whereas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1034bf5806c189c73e68ae42d79c84045be9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{N000}$\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> cannot be a square. This means, we must find a square, such that the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits are close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, but not there, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0a3589706a0df340ebe663e060a8d5448a915c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$961$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/33299fd8cf4e0b5dab838160226e36e05c9279bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$974$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. Now, the best we can do is to keep on listing squares until we hit one that fits. We do not need to solve for each square: remember that the difference between consecutive squares are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8fc82e121c01034fef87ac28f73e7d4c0b465c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, so all we need to do is addition. After making a list, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04525d80591cd8f04aa2fd30d40d4e5081ca395b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$531^2=281961$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e5f9297dbfdb360de90aa061921ccccaf7193c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$532^2=283024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />. It skipped <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0238be457166bbb26da8b0a21f302283436d5e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$282000$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e20fae0eb42a95938d8707fc356616893c9b43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{282}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number being squared. Based on the reasoning above, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39b14023c98c943554d150561aacc188c4ce26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43160c3eb23bbf35bd9b7952ab57e8f9cb5db24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-500$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />. We can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d9c39132ab8cb7f40a067af508ff77e95df3d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(500+k)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"19\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/470fc78173dfeb81591d2804d2664a8a286ecede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250000+1000k+k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" />. We can disregard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/5/085582a9ce8c4388675b5ecd883cc1f9f06789d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250000$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bbce23dd61183e2baed349d8426da7d6bdb2e34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, since they won't affect the last three digits, which determines if there are any squares between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c39e05ef603ddb6ac6101e71cb8186d74795b3ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{N000}\\rightarrow \\overline{N999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />. So we must find a square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />, such that it is under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, but the next square is over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737bf9b9ddaf4d4879ecdb1dbf30e8080954c19f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/8260841e48449a4547e34c90e614e9d4ce4c368a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2=961$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cacc6087cc0d77e25def9079f6eff2fd3a85eda5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1)^2=32^2=1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"19\" />. We can be sure that this skips a thousand because the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bbce23dd61183e2baed349d8426da7d6bdb2e34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> increments it up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> each time. Now we can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f6243e98bc3ea1393c52e1990b4626f7434aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(500+31)^2=281961$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/272914ef8bdae9c9ceb8cf45db66b58be8722459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(500+32)^2=283024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"19\" />. We skipped <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0238be457166bbb26da8b0a21f302283436d5e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$282000$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e20fae0eb42a95938d8707fc356616893c9b43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{282}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The goal is to find the least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d4dca7148efdbd28a438a71982603a99461287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/6/146f26abdfb319b78cfb6127d2d766213f4adacb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists m \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/82678ad30147cf7641a4d93be56718a411b661a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 + 1 \\leq 1000N, 1000N + 1000 \\leq (m+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"345\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nCombining the two inequalities leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f17a335766406133d3b175d04394420b585d411c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m+1)^2 \\geq m^2 + 1001, m \\geq 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4ca5ad0957849ebcf2d75c126a1aaf06ed4cd43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = k + 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2aab33165e365605fe272690d463631c708c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{W}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, then the inequalities become,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd748e7cad1db265a26e8df76b53a2b0150e8d52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\geq \\frac{(k+500)^2 + 1}{1000} = \\frac{k^2 + 1}{1000} + k + 250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"318\" height=\"41\" />, and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07e4e929a56bb3e1431532ef416e0d5dc20c25c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\leq \\frac{(k+501)^2}{1000} - 1 = \\frac{(k+1)^2}{1000} + k + 250.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"337\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737bf9b9ddaf4d4879ecdb1dbf30e8080954c19f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, one can verify that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197b6be4fa2f42299a0897d575da4b539ef496b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 282$\" width=\"67\" height=\"12\" /> is the unique integer satisfying the inequalities.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/25313d6c9abf27ffd5e6cf8d59e3718ac5b6ec43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\leq 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82dad8ca587b1793a162b8d53f2c62a13424b946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 250 &lt; \\frac{k^2 + 1}{1000} + k + 250 \\leq N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"261\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf7f177ddb4a1c1e26ea80e3ad0c83d730b7b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq \\frac{(k+1)^2}{1000} + k + 250 \\leq \\frac{(30+1)^2}{1000} + k + 250 &lt; k + 251$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"435\" height=\"41\" />, \n</p><p>i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123a8f0e2a3332aa248f813739306377e69b0768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 250 &lt; N &lt; k + 251$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"16\" />, a contradiction. \n</p><p>Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d16a6ed1c91543b8184e8bcc97376c72549747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> leads to larger <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />(s).\n</p><p>Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e20fae0eb42a95938d8707fc356616893c9b43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{282}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~yuxiaomatt\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Rjx-0hAfQ6E?si=sr0N7dWeMg1jH5Bq\">https://youtu.be/Rjx-0hAfQ6E?si=sr0N7dWeMg1jH5Bq</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Very similar to 2016 AMC 12 A Problem 25: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/2016_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/2016_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II\" title=\"2013 AIME II\">2013 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042616\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.065 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.084 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 580/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17427/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.362      1 -total\n 55.15%    7.369      1 Template:AIME_box\n 43.11%    5.760      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11891:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017042616 and revision id 237950. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}